WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:04.470
Pairing buddy is an AI pair programmer for Neovim.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:07.240
Here are three moments from an ordinary day.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:11.850
You edit the wrong file while a test is red.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:13.160
Watch the margin.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.640
You change the backoff.

00:00:23.508 --> 00:00:26.468
Pair speaks once, under your line.

00:00:26.468 --> 00:00:29.818
The real cause is in worker dot go.

00:00:29.818 --> 00:00:31.488
Alt J goes there.

00:00:37.238 --> 00:00:39.818
You fix one line, and save.

00:00:39.818 --> 00:00:42.928
Watch the statusline, then the ghost text.

00:00:44.398 --> 00:00:47.828
Pair runs your tests on every save.

00:00:47.828 --> 00:00:51.198
A test that passed before now fails.

00:00:53.218 --> 00:00:56.778
Alt J shows Pair’s fix as ghost text:

00:00:56.778 --> 00:01:00.788
the old line struck through, the new one under it.

00:01:00.788 --> 00:01:02.488
Alt Y takes it.

00:01:02.488 --> 00:01:04.238
Save, and it’s green.

00:01:08.128 --> 00:01:10.488
You hand Pair the wheel for one change.

00:01:10.488 --> 00:01:11.998
Watch your code.

00:01:13.548 --> 00:01:16.058
Pair drive, and say what you want.

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:26.251
It types where you can see it, tests the unsaved buffer, and hands back.

00:01:29.601 --> 00:01:32.691
U undoes it all, in one step.

00:01:36.581 --> 00:01:37.901
Pairing buddy.

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:41.911
The full tutorial, the docs and the code are on GitHub.
